{
    "dex.aurorale": "The aurora is the sky remembering the buried verse; Aurorale is the only one who can hum along without forgetting it again.",
    "dex.barrowmoss": "A barrow that got up. The verse buried under it got up too, and they have not yet agreed who carries whom.",
    "dex.bogboar": "It charges through the fen on a war-grunt in 6/8. Fenwick's palisade is less a wall than a suggestion.",
    "dex.brackaw": "Its cackle curdles milk and morale alike. Skald sailors swear it learned harmony purely to ruin it.",
    "dex.brinemare": "A foam-maned gallop that herds cod the way dogs herd sheep, whistling the work as it goes.",
    "dex.cobbelt": "Varde's streets are paved with its molted plates. It collects the toll in whistled thirds.",
    "dex.dirgelk": "It walks the cairn lines at dusk carrying antlers full of candle-ice. Mourners follow at a grateful distance.",
    "dex.eiderdun": "Its down holds the warmth of every song sung near it. Skald cradles are lined with molted verses.",
    "dex.emberjarl": "It keeps the longhouse hearth as a point of honor and duels draughts to the death.",
    "dex.fiddlefox": "It dances payment out of market crowds and tips its tail like a hat. Varde pretends to disapprove.",
    "dex.fjordrake": "It rides the standing wave at the fjord mouth for the joy of the bass line. Ships time their entrances to its verses.",
    "dex.frostfiddle": "Its ribs bow against the cold like strings. On clear nights the whole flock tunes to the aurora.",
    "dex.glimmwyrm": "It surfaces in the fjord on still nights to rehearse with its own reflection, in canon.",
    "dex.gullnote": "It steals refrains instead of chips, repeating them a fourth higher out of pure cheek.",
    "dex.henge": "A standing stone from the verse-circle, still keeping its beat. The other eleven are listening for it.",
    "dex.hulderbuck": "Beautiful from the front, birch-bark hollow from behind. It trades verses for butter and always pays short.",
    "dex.jokulhorn": "A glacier calf with the patience of its parent and the temper of neither.",
    "dex.kragveld": "A scarp with opinions about the weather, most of them downdrafts. The pass closes when it sings flat.",
    "dex.loomgarde": "Its warp threads are wire, its weft is ivy, and the cloth it weaves hums lullabies for a week off the loom.",
    "dex.mireling": "It gargles bog-water to tune itself. The tune is filthy. It is very proud.",
    "dex.morrowflame": "Lit from the last ember of the verse-circle's last gathering. It has been carried, never owned, for nine hundred years.",
    "dex.nokkelpie": "It plays the fjord like a glass harp and drowns only critics. So it claims.",
    "dex.peatling": "Cut it like turf and it regrows whistling. Fenwick hearths burn only what volunteers.",
    "dex.reynardeau": "The fiddler the dance follows. It has stolen every show in Skalden and returned each one slightly improved.",
    "dex.rimeram": "It headbutts avalanches into rhythm. Kraghorn's lift system is four of them and a prayer.",
    "dex.runolf": "It carries the rune for 'refrain' scarred on its flank — nobody remembers cutting it, least of all Runolf.",
    "dex.saltlick": "A tidepool boulder that learned patience from both teachers. Fjord cattle worship it, lickingly.",
    "dex.screel": "It sharpens its own edges on the wind. Kraghorn shepherds shear them for whetstones each spring.",
    "dex.skaldgeir": "The verse-circle's tuning spear, still upright where the twelfth stone fell. It answers questions in key signatures.",
    "dex.skarnbjorn": "The mountain's foreman. It signs no contracts and honors all of them, shift bell to shift bell.",
    "dex.skerrald": "Its shell is a drowned bell recast by barnacle patience. Harbormasters set the tide-tables to its yawn.",
    "dex.skerryn": "It naps in net-floats and pays rent in foghorn harmonies. Skald fishers count a boat unlucky without one.",
    "dex.spindrel": "A dropped spindle that kept the rhythm of the wheel. Varde's weavers apprentice them before children.",
    "dex.tindrelod": "It rings the aurora down the lightning rods of Kraghorn and bills nobody, which worries the council.",
    "dex.turfowl": "It nests in sod roofs and pays the household in weather warnings, two hoots flat for rain.",
    "dex.velkomma": "It blooms exactly once a winter, at the door of whoever most needs proof that spring is real.",
    "dex.vinterstem": "The buried verse itself, wearing winter as a body. When Skalden sings together it stands very still and listens back.",
    "dex.voltvarg": "Storm-pack runner; the howl arrives a half-second after the flash. Kraghorn sets its clocks by the pack.",
    "dex.waeverin": "It weaves hedgerows into staves and plants the year's weather in them as notation.",
    "dex.willowail": "It mourns professionally — hired by villages that lost their own verse and need one carried in.",
