    "npc.verse_keeper_4": "Verse Keeper",
    "region.skalden": "Skalden",
    "skald.ferry.back": "Ode: Back to Cantorel it is. The fjord hums you out — that's new, that is.",
    "skald.ferry.locked": "Ode: Boat goes when the song holds steady. It doesn't, yet. You'd know more about that than me, I reckon.",
    "skald.ferry.out": "Ode: Borders open, song willing. Skalden, then — mind the gulls, they steal refrains.",
    "skald.hall1.after": "Brimhild: Varde next. Vevstad weaves; don't blink.",
    "skald.hall1.badge": "Brimhild: The Tide Mark, first of four.",
    "skald.hall1.defeat": "Brimhild: Held! The first line is yours: 'Low under keel and key—'",
    "skald.hall1.intro": "Brimhild: First line of the verse keeps the tide honest. Show me you can hold a line against water.",
    "skald.hall2.after": "Vevstad: The Hollow keeps the third line. Myrra keeps the Hollow.",
    "skald.hall2.badge": "Vevstad: The Loom Mark, second of four.",
    "skald.hall2.defeat": "Vevstad: Unpicked! Take it: '—the loom remembers what we lost—'",
    "skald.hall2.early": "Vevstad: Order matters in a verse. Brimhild first.",
    "skald.hall2.intro": "Vevstad: Second line binds the warp to the weft. Unpick me if you can.",
    "skald.hall3.after": "Myrra: Kraghorn, then. Aldis has been waiting longer than the rest of us put together.",
    "skald.hall3.badge": "Myrra: The Barrow Mark, third of four.",
    "skald.hall3.defeat": "Myrra: …Gently enough. The third line: '—buried not to silence but to save—'",
    "skald.hall3.early": "Myrra: The bog eats verses sung out of order. Vevstad first.",
    "skald.hall3.intro": "Myrra: Third line sleeps in the barrow. Wake it gently or not at all.",
    "skald.hall4.after": "Aldis: The verse is whole and the sky's in key. Stay for a winter sometime.",
    "skald.hall4.badge": "Aldis: The Aurora Mark. Four of four — the verse is yours to carry now.",
    "skald.hall4.defeat": "Aldis: HA! The aurora was right about you.",
    "skald.hall4.early": "Aldis: Three lines before the fourth. The mountain insists.",
    "skald.hall4.intro": "Aldis: The last line I'll not say — I'll PLAY it. Keep up if you're the one the aurora's been on about.",
    "skald.verse.1": "Aldis: 'Low under keel and key — the loom remembers what we lost — buried not to silence but to save — and sung again when one voice carries all.'",
    "skald.verse.2": "Aldis: Your Chorus, our verse. Same song, friend. It always was.",
    "skald.verse.found": "Four lines, one verse, and the aurora finally singing on-key. You did that. Skalden remembers who sings with it.",
    "skald.verse.hint": "Long before your eight bells, Skalden buried a verse too dangerous to sing and split the key between four keepers. Ask them in order; they're traditional about it.",
